Z||000000||Red Toyota MR2||02-18-2001||12:54 AM||||Hello everyone.<P>My 84 2M4 Fiero is getting horrid gas milage.  My 67 Chevy pickup does better.  What could this be?  I have replaced the O2 sensor, plugs, wires (MSD) Coil (MSD) cap and rotor.  The car only has 122K miles on it, and runs like crap, thinking some sensors are bad.  The check engine light IS on, but only part time.  <P>What terminals do I short to read codes, and what do they meen?  I am new to the Fiero world, and really dont like the motor in the car.  Then again, 4Cyl's should always be DOHC, not push rod!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Is there any cheap things I can do to the car to make it faster?  I dont want to dump alot of money into it, as the body is bad (wrecked twice) and has a salvage title.<P>Thanks for any info<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||02-18-2001||10:28 AM||||Check your EGR valve.......K&N air filter...Low temp thermostat...poly dog bone...for some cheap and good performance upgrades.<P>Oh Yeah.....you should probably post questions like this in the Technical section.<p>[This message has been edited by 2M4 Dale (edited 02-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||02-18-2001||11:08 AM||||The connector for the trouble codes is in the center console next to the Cig. lighter. It takes a torx bit to get the 2 screws out that hold the panel. the 2 you jump are on the bottom passenger's side of the connector.<P>Just jump that and turn the key to run and watch the code.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
